4. Non-Commercial Restriction

The covered SWI materials may not be used for commercial purposes without prior written authorization from the copyright holder or an authority expressly designated by the copyright holder.

Commercial use includes, but is not limited to:

- selling the software;
- selling products or services substantially based on the covered SWI implementation;
- offering SWI functionality as a paid service;
- incorporating covered SWI code into a commercial product;
- using covered SWI implementation as a commercial backend or infrastructure component;
- licensing the covered SWI materials to customers for commercial exploitation;
- using the covered SWI implementation to provide paid services to third parties;
- commercially distributing modified versions;
- monetising a hosted or managed implementation substantially incorporating covered SWI code.

Commercial use requires separate written authorization.

Authorization may be granted on conditions determined by the copyright holder.

Nothing in this section prevents a person from conducting ordinary non-commercial research, education, testing, review, or experimentation merely because the person or organisation also conducts commercial activities elsewhere.

