5. Written Authorization

Commercial authorization must be granted in writing.

A public statement, repository fork, issue comment, informal discussion, social-media post, presentation, or verbal statement does not by itself constitute commercial authorization unless it expressly identifies the intended commercial permission and is issued by an authorized representative.

Commercial authorization may specify permitted product or service, modules, territory, duration, distribution model, attribution, commercial terms, contribution requirements, security or governance requirements, and other conditions.

