8. Provenance and Legacy

SWI is an evolving body of work.

Copies, forks, derivatives, adaptations, and implementations based on the covered materials must not intentionally erase or falsify the documented provenance of the original SWI work.

A person may describe their own contributions, modifications, research, or independent implementation as their own work.

However, such descriptions must not falsely state or imply that the original SWI materials were independently created by that person when they were derived from the covered repository.

The existence of a fork does not transfer authorship of the original repository.

The existence of a derivative implementation does not transfer copyright in the original materials.

