11. Originality and Attribution

The recipient must not knowingly make a false representation that the original SWI repository, its original documentation, or its original copyrighted implementation was authored by the recipient or by another party when the material was obtained from the SWI project.

A recipient may identify their own implementation, research, modifications, experiments, extensions, tests, integrations, and independent discoveries, distinguishing those contributions from the original SWI work.

